 "lines": [
  {
   "shot": 1,
   "start": 0.0,
   "at": 0.3,
   "dur": 8.5,
   "text": "Companies pay a frontier model for every coding call, even FizzBuzz. Chimera answers each call at the cheapest place that gets it right."
  },
  {
   "shot": 2,
   "start": 9.55,
   "at": 9.85,
   "dur": 12.12,
   "text": "This take is live, on our own graphics card. I hold W and walk up to the gates. I look left, and left again. One click, and the gates swing open. Then the great door, and the Great Hall."
  },
  {
   "shot": 3,
   "start": 23.82,
   "at": 24.12,
   "dur": 19.78,
   "text": "I ask the Count a question. The call climbs a ladder. First our shared cache, then our own thirty billion model, then the big seven hundred sixty-three billion model. The cache has not seen this question. So our thirty billion model answers, on our own card, in about a second. No token bill."
  },
  {
   "shot": 4,
   "start": 44.66,
   "at": 44.96,
   "dur": 9.15,
   "text": "I ask the same question again. This time the shared cache answers, in a fraction of a second. Zero tokens, and no model was called."
  },
  {
   "shot": 5,
   "start": 54.91,
   "at": 55.21,
   "dur": 6.55,
   "text": "Now FizzBuzz. Our thirty billion model writes it in a second or two, and every token stays off the big model."
  },
  {
   "shot": 6,
   "start": 64.01,
   "at": 64.31,
   "dur": 17.55,
   "text": "Now a hard design task. The thirty billion model tries first, but it is not sure enough. So the call climbs to the seven hundred sixty-three billion model. Here is a loss. With the climb, this call is slower than asking the big model alone, at about the same cost."
  },
  {
   "shot": 7,
   "start": 83.06,
   "at": 83.36,
   "dur": 19.74,
   "text": "Here is the bill for a month of coding calls. When three in ten calls are repeats, we spend sixty-two to eighty-seven percent less than G P T five point five alone. Now the loss. Against the cheap seven hundred sixty-three billion model, at a hundred thousand calls a day, we cost six hundred seven percent more."
  },
  {
   "shot": 8,
   "start": 103.85,
   "at": 104.15,
   "dur": 14.07,
   "text": "We built this with Kiro. Seven steering files, seven specs, six hooks, four custom agents, M C P tools and a Power. Property tests from the specs found four real bugs, and all four are fixed."
  },
  {
   "shot": 9,
   "start": 119.02,
   "at": 119.32,
   "dur": 4.18,
   "text": "Stop paying a frontier model for FizzBuzz. We prove it with tests."
  },
  {
   "shot": 10,
   "start": 124.3,
   "at": 124.6,
   "dur": 19.04,
   "text": "On our own A six thousand card, calls to the seven hundred sixty-three billion model fell seventy point seven percent, with zero wrong answers from the cache. We got two hundred ninety-two of three hundred one coding tasks right. The big model alone got two hundred eighty-six. The loss: a first pass is slower."
  }
 ],
